EXT. GOLD RUSH DENTIST TENT - SIERRA FOOTHILLS - 1851 - DUSK

A canvas tent on a muddy hill. Lanterns. A sign in shaky paint: "TEETH PULLED. 2 DOLLARS. NO CREDIT."

INT. DENTIST TENT - CONTINUOUS

A barber's chair nailed to a plank floor. A tray of forceps. A bottle of whiskey and a bucket.

DR. EZEKIEL "ZEKE" MONTAGUE, 50s, in a stained vest, leans over the chair. In the chair, a miner, ABNER TWOBEARS, 40s, white-knuckled, mouth wide.

ZEKE
Hold still.

ABNER
(muffled)
I'm holding.

ZEKE
You're trembling.

ABNER
(muffled)
I'm holding while trembling.

Zeke lifts the forceps. Peers into the mouth. Sniffs.

ZEKE
This one's rotten.

ABNER
(muffled)
Pull it.

ZEKE
You sure?

ABNER
(muffled)
He's been pulling at me for three weeks. Pull it.

Zeke grips. Twists. Pulls. The tooth pops. Abner howls. Zeke holds it up to the lantern.

ZEKE
Eighteen karat.

ABNER
(spitting)
What?

ZEKE
It's gold. Your tooth is gold.

Abner reaches up and feels his jaw. Then looks at Zeke.

ABNER
Give it back.

ZEKE
It's my fee.

ABNER
It's my tooth.

ZEKE
It was your tooth. Now it's a fee.

Abner rises. Fists clench. Zeke steps back, tooth in hand.

ABNER
Hand it over, Doc.

ZEKE
Two dollars, Abner.

ABNER
I'll give you the two dollars.

ZEKE
And the tooth.

ABNER
And the tooth stays mine.

A long silence. Then Zeke tosses the tooth. Abner catches it. Pays two coins. They both exhale.

ZEKE
Next time, I'll price by the karat.

ABNER
Next time, I'll pull my own.

He pockets the tooth, tips his hat, and leaves. Zeke watches him go. The lantern hisses. Outside, a mule brays. He pours himself a drink.

ZEKE (CONT'D)
(to the empty chair)
Next.

The tent flap opens on wind and dark.
